    },
    {
      "id": "claim_57ca4c78484f4e07bef6149cdc93d951",
      "statement": "Each analysis pass writes case-level evidence to resultados/evidencia/<secao>_<analise>/, prefixed by the section number of the notebook that generated it, containing casos.csv (rule-selected cases), leia-me.md, crus/ (the unmodified raw trace row) and derivados/ (per-case derived tables/views); generation is two-stage (the notebook writes the structural part, then a drill-down script writes crus/ and the derived views, checking each excerpt against the raw row as it writes).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://analysis/2026-09-trace-law-flow/README.md#L73-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e5ce154dd9003f771ca340f2bfd57b85de5830d654264894810ab258907cb0f1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_99042d6e190a44dab9c4bb1f5c684640",
      "statement": "The validation procedure requires recomputing key numbers via a genuinely different code path (not reusing the same classification function or notebook) as proof a number isn't an artifact of one specific logic bug; one such independent recomputation using plain csv.DictReader (no pandas) matched the notebook's reported count exactly.",
      "evidence": [
