    {
      "id": "claim_ff84020356294e14aa921195a1432f04",
      "statement": "A robustness test on the analysis's most important recurrence number showed it was not robust to the matching heuristic used: substring correspondence by message prefix gave 13.7% while suffix correspondence gave 4.3%, and investigating concrete examples via drill_down.py showed the prefix method was catching generic exception boilerplate rather than the specific error — the taxonomy-category method (11.9%) was adopted as correct.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://analysis/2026-09-trace-law-flow/docs/03-procedimento-validacao.md#L78-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ae5d7819023d54d2e1297a96918588a297ad540776b8d12108cd10404db4c095:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_780828ced3af41889281afa8c6616cf6",
      "statement": "The project's criterion for when a finding needs a robustness test is whether the number depends on an arbitrary analytical choice: direct counts (tokens per execution, trajectories ending in error, propagation coefficient, error rate per role) are robust by construction and need no test, while any number embedding a 'what counts as the same' decision does.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://analysis/2026-09-trace-law-flow/docs/03-procedimento-validacao.md#L111-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad5755ccc7b081b808872d123717d690dd32003f66037f9b18e3760710382b99:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_42be5ae8d4e4412ba7d927ec5059f468",
      "statement": "A dated analysis folder that hosts more than one methodologically distinct analysis organizes each as a 'passe' (pass): a pre-registered method applied to a set of units, sharing one notebook per pass regardless of how many units share that method, built on a shared base_pipeline.py rather than duplicating notebook cells.",
